==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|palliatif|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|NL.|en}} *palliativus, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|palliare||to cloak}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|pallium|lang=la||a cloak}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpalɪətɪv/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Serving to palliate; serving to extenuate or mitigate.
# {{context|medicine|lang=en}} Minimising the progression of a [[disease]] and relieving [[undesirable]] [[symptoms]] for as long as possible, rather than attempting to cure the (usually [[incurable]]) disease.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|medicine}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{sense|medicine}} [[analgesic]], [[lenitive]]

====Related terms====
* [[palliate]]
* [[palliation]]

